# Crustum Mongo Migrations

## Documentation First

Prefer the migrations docs (`docs/ODM/migrations/**`) — especially [Creating
Migrations](docs/ODM/migrations/getting-started/creating-migrations), [Writing
Migrations](docs/ODM/migrations/guides/writing-migrations), and [Snapshots and
Diffs](docs/ODM/migrations/getting-started/snapshots-and-diffs) — as the full
reference. This skill is the fast orientation. Use the `bake-development` skill
for `bake mongo_model` / `bake document` etc.

## Command Names (Mongo, not cake)

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo migrations migrate') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo migrations rollback') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo migrations status') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo migrations mark_migrated') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo migrations reset') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('mongo schema dump') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mongo_migration CreateProducts') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mongo_migration_diff Name') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mongo_migration_snapshot Initial') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mongo_seed Users') }}
```

There is no `bin/cake migrations ...` or `bake migration` here — the commands
are namespaced `mongo` / `mongo_*`. Migration files live in `config/MongoMigrations/`
(`YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_Name.php`), seeds in `config/MongoSeeds/`.

## Migration Class

Extend `Crustum\Mongo\Migration\BaseMigration`. Prefer `change()` for
reversible migrations; use `up()`/`down()` for irreversible steps.

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Crustum\Mongo\Migration\BaseMigration;

class CreateProducts extends BaseMigration
{
    public function change(): void
    {
        $collection = $this->collection('products');
        $collection->addColumn('name', 'string', ['length' => 255]);
        $collection->addColumn('user_id', 'objectid');
        $collection->addColumn('price', 'decimal128');
        $collection->addColumn('created', 'date');
        $collection->addColumn('modified', 'date');
        $collection->addIndex(['slug' => 1], ['unique' => true]);
        $collection->create();
    }
}
```

### Collection builder (`Db\Collection`)

- Terminators: `create()` (new collection), `update()` (existing), `drop()` →
  `create()` (drop a collection).
- Fields: `addColumn()` / `addField()` (alias), `removeField()`, `hasField()`.
- Indexes: `addIndex(['field' => 1], ['unique' => true])`, `removeIndex($name)`.
  Keys are Mongo key maps (`['field' => 1]`), not cake arrays.
- Validator: `setValidator(['$jsonSchema' => [...]])` (fields/constraints on a
  collection are expressed via the `$jsonSchema` validator, not SQL DDL).
- BaseMigration helpers: `collection()`, `hasCollection()`, `listCollections()`,
  `createCollection()`, `dropCollection()`, `renameCollection()`, `index()`,
  `uniqueIndex()`, `dropIndex()`, `setValidator()`.

## Field Types (Mongo canonical)

`objectid` (any `*_id`/`id`), `string`, `text`, `integer`, `int64`,
`decimal128`, `boolean`, `date`, `timestamp`, `binary`, `uuid`, `hash`, `array`,
`collection`, `raw`. `created`/`modified`/`updated` infer to `date` (not
`datetime`). There is no SQL `varchar`/`int(11)`; use the Mongo spellings.

## Bake Column Grammar

`fieldName:fieldType?[length]:default[value]:unique`

- `?` = nullable; `[length]` = length or `[precision,scale]` for decimals;
- `default[value]` = default (bool/int/float/string/null);
- `:unique` = unique index.
- Inferred: `*_id`→`objectid`, `created/modified/updated`→`date`,
  `lat/lng/latitude/longitude`→`decimal128`, else `string`.

Name prefixes drive generated code: `Create*`, `Drop*`, `Add*To*`,
`Remove*From*`, `Alter*On*`, `Alter*`. `Add*To*` / `Alter*On*` emit
`addColumn(...)->update()`; there is **no** `changeColumn` (alter = re-add the
field + `update()`). `Remove*From*` emits `removeField()` (irreversible → use
`up()`/`down()`).

## Reversibility

`change()` is reversed automatically via a `RecordingAdapter` that inverts the
recorded actions. `removeField()` is not reversible — put it in `up()` and add a
matching `addColumn()` in `down()`. Anonymous migration classes are **not**
supported (named classes only).

## Snapshot / Diff / Dump

- `bake mongo_migration_snapshot Initial` — snapshot current DB into a
  migration; auto-marks migrated unless `--generate-only`.
- `bake mongo_migration_diff Name` — diff live schema vs dump file → migration.
- `mongo schema dump` — writes `config/MongoMigrations/schema-dump-mongo.lock`.
  Diff cannot detect field renames.
- Common options: `-p/--plugin`, `-c/--connection`, `-s/--source`;
  `--generate-only`, `--no-lock` on snapshot/diff.

## Tracking

- Migration journal: `cake_migrations` collection (unique `(version, plugin)`
  index; plugin-tagged so app + plugin migrations coexist).
- Seeds tracked in `_seeds` (unique `(seed_name, plugin)` index); idempotent
  seeds re-run, non-idempotent run once.
- `bake mongo_model` and schema listing skip `cake_migrations` / `_seeds`.

## Common Pitfalls

- Using cake commands (`migrations migrate`, `bake migration`) — use the `mongo`
  / `mongo_*` variants.
- `integer`/`varchar`/`datetime` SQL types — use `int64`/`string`/`date`.
- Foreign-key-style columns typed `int` — an `*_id` field must be `objectid`.
- Indexes as cake arrays (`['slug']`) — use key maps (`['slug' => 1]`).
- Forgetting a terminator (`create()`/`update()`/`drop()->create()`).
- `removeField()` inside `change()` (irreversible).
- Not running `mongo migrations migrate` after baking.
